{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-1c06809d1db669570103","statement":"Let $f:X\\to S$ be a morphism of schemes of finite type over $k$. An $\\ell$-adic complex $\\mF$ on $X$ is called locally acyclic with respect to $f$ if for every geometric point $x\\in X$, and every geometric point $t\\in S_{(f(x))}$, the natural map $R\\Gamma(X_{(x)},\\mF)\\to R\\Gamma( (X_{(x)})_t,\\mF)$ is an isomorphism, where $(X_{(x)})_t=X_{(x)}\\times_{S_{(f(x))}}t$. It is called universally locally acyclic (ULA) if it is locally acyclic after arbitrary base change $S'\\to S$.","source_id":"arXiv:1603.05593","cluster":"algebraic_geometry","statement_sha256":"6dd2102c4b444de8c206f77d42a592abc33aa5dcea0b19ba32cf9bd7b4c1d459","kind":"definition","label":"Definition 207","ref_key":"","name":"","order":254,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05593","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"9aa0de800bec9f56ae36a0522194f91bc11ab1fe49bff0d4068568a9eb549a68","line":3546,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-27T16:49:20+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":477,"math_hints":42}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1603.05593","title":"Guide for Lecturers in the Park City Mathematics Institute","abstract":"We introduce various affine Grassmannians, study their geometric properties, and give some applications. We also discuss the geometric Satake equivalence. These are the expanded lecture notes for a mini-course in 2015 PCMI summer school. References updated and more details added.","authors":["Xinwen Zhu"],"year":"2016","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05593","cluster":"algebraic_geometry","macros":{"on":"\\operatorname","fraka":"{\\mathfrak a}","frakg":"{\\mathfrak g}","frakl":"{\\mathfrak l}","frakp":"{\\mathfrak p}","frakq":"{\\mathfrak q}","fraks":"{\\mathfrak s}","frakt":"{\\mathfrak t}","bA":"{\\mathbb A}"